      "writtenOn": "2021-05-10T14:03:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Having a fairly generally-useful Rust crate like this here, complete with Cargo.toml and everything, feels like the wrong place. Maybe it belongs under external/rust? When I recently wanted to do something similar (for the command-fds crate) the recommendation from the Rusty Droids chat was to publish it as a separate open source project, publish to crates.io, and then import back to Android under external/rust/crates using the standard process. That does have more overhead though. It would be good to talk to the Android Rust team about how best to handle situations like this, if you haven\u0027t already.",
      "revId": "9bb8d3618d93adb0a16785abb8fca83cd63720bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8a665433_c4edc55a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-10T14:52:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the future, this could evolve into a general rust implementation of fuse-over-zip, but I don\u0027t have an immediate plan to do so. Doing so will only complicate the code a lot, especially for supporting write operations. In addition, this depends on libfuse-rs which is a crate that belongs to crosvm. So, I don\u0027t think this qualifies to be in external/rust (at least yet).\n\ncargo.toml was added just to accelerate my development cycle. (`atest` is way slower than `cargo test`). That will eventually be disappear though.\n\nFurthermore, next rounds of CLs will put microdroid-specific changes like mounting zip over dm-verity. That in theory could be done in a separate program but I\u0027d like to do that in the same binary to keep the size minimal.",
      "parentUuid": "30600093_efe6caa6",
      "revId": "9bb8d3618d93adb0a16785abb8fca83cd63720bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
