      "writtenOn": "2021-05-10T20:06:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is fine for now, but just checking.  Are we going to always keep the whole executable in memory?\n\nIf the goal is to share buffer between open\u0027ed files, I suspect the filesystem cache already takes care of this.  FUSE could know the files are backed by the same inode judging from what `lookup` returns (though I\u0027m not entirely sure).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 200,
        "endChar": 75
