      "lineNbr": 200,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-10T23:45:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For compressed entries, yes, for uncompressed entries, no. And I\u0027d like to encourage (or even mandate) that executables are stored uncompressed to make XIP possible.\n\nThe reason to have this buffer is because we need to decompress an entry in order to support the read semantics - read `size` amount of data at `offset`. If we don\u0027t have this buffer, every read operations would require decompression of the entire entry, which would be very inefficient.",
      "parentUuid": "7d6b65b6_2f6cdf92",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 200,
        "endChar": 75
